// The old spelling is reserved for exactly one job: naming the new one. Burxt spells
// every keyword the word it means, which is why `allocates` and `decreases` were never
// `alloc` and `dec` — and why `fn` should not have been `fn`.
fn total(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {
    return a + b;
}
print(total(1, 2));
